# Playwright storageState / auth-state files (B-323 round 4). These are written by the
# live-gate scripts and contain a REAL bearer token in localStorage. One of them
# (agents/orch-b-recon/b323-proof/baseline-impact/state.json) reached a COMMIT as a side
# effect of a script whose output dir happens to be tracked — a credential landed in the
# repo because nobody chose to put it there. Ignore the SHAPE, not that one path:
# every sibling script already writes its state file to /tmp or a scratch dir, and this
# keeps the next one from having to remember.
*state.json
*storage-state.json
*auth-state.json

# --- credential-bearing test material (2026-09-07) -----------------------------
# The hand-test manual and its workbook now carry the LIVE staging login for all
# 12 seed accounts, because a tester needs to read one row and sign in. This repo
# is public, so a single `git add -A` would publish that password to GitHub — the
# exact shape of B-419, which cost a rotation on a box that was already on the
# internet. Ignore the material, not just these two names: anything under the
# recon folder that is a manual or a workbook is assumed to carry credentials.
/agents/orch-b-recon/user-test-manual.md
/agents/orch-b-recon/*-manual.md
/agents/orch-b-recon/*.xlsx
